-      "description": "What: Implement the immutable version-1 observation, usage, summary, failure vocabulary, validation, sanitization, and record conversion.\n\nLocation:\n- src/ovcaq/events/model.py\n- src/ovcaq/events/__init__.py\n\nReuse:\n- src/ovcaq/state/schema.py validation rules where dependency direction permits; otherwise mirror the small neutral primitive.\n\nContract:\nPROTOCOL_VERSION: Final[int] = 1\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass Usage:\n    input_tokens: int | None = None\n    output_tokens: int | None = None\n    cache_creation_input_tokens: int | None = None\n    cache_read_input_tokens: int | None = None\n    tool_uses: int | None = None\n    cost_usd: float | None = None\n    estimated: bool = False\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass Observation:\n    protocol_version: int\n    timestamp: datetime\n    provider: str\n    run_id: str\n    session_id: str | None\n    lane_id: str | None\n    type: ObservationType\n    payload: Mapping[str, FrozenJSONValue]\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nclass SessionSummary:\n    success: bool\n    session_id: str | None\n    failure_class: FailureClass | None\n    failure_detail: str | None\n    rate_limit_reset_at: datetime | None\n    usage: Usage | None\n\ndef observation_record(observation: Observation) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\ndef observation_from_record(record: object) -> Observation: ...\ndef summary_record(summary: SessionSummary) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\ndef sanitize_text(value: str) -> str: ...\ndef sanitize_json(value: JSONValue) -> JSONValue: ...\n\nDetails:\n- Implement the complete ObservationType and FailureClass members specified by the design.\n- Deep-freeze and sanitize payloads at construction and again at serialization; validate version, UTC timestamps, identifiers, and numeric usage.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [P04-T01] Define `Observation`, `Usage`, `SessionSummary`, and failure classes.\n- Protocol tests prove total decoding and provider-neutral data.\n- [ ] Unknown input yields observable raw fallback, never a decoder crash.\n\nVerify: Run focused event model tests, Ruff, and mypy.",
+      "name": "Implement pure supervisor decisions and progress snapshots",
+      "description": "Implement pure supervisor decisions and progress snapshots\n\nImplement immutable supervisor policy/snapshot/result/retry/decision records, workflow-only fingerprints, and the ordered pure decision table. Keep provider output and final prose out of every input.\n\nLocation: src/ovcaq/runtime/decision.py; src/ovcaq/runtime/__init__.py\n\nReuse: src/ovcaq/state/schema.py state records, src/ovcaq/events/model.py SessionSummary, workflow phase/status enums, and the legacy decision characterization cases.\n\nContract (verbatim \u2014 from the design doc's `## Interfaces & contracts`):\n- `DecisionKind`: `PAUSE`, `RUN_CAPABILITY`, `SKIP_CAPABILITIES`, `COMPLETE`, `CONTINUE`, `WAIT`, `RETRY`, `PARK`, `HALT`.\n- `SupervisorPolicy`: `died_retries`, `connectivity_retries`, `rate_limit_retries`, `connectivity_wait_seconds`, `rate_limit_wait_seconds`, `phase_repeat_limit`.\n- `ProgressSnapshot`: `revision`, `batch_id`, `batch_status`, `prd`, `phase`, `next_phase`, `pause_requested`, `pause_reason`, `attention`, `recovery_operation`, `tasks_completed`, `review_cycle`, `completed_prds`, `drained`, `capabilities`, `phase_fingerprint`, `phase_repeats`.\n- `AttemptResult`: `summary`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `state_after`, `state_error`.\n- `RetryState`: `died`, `connectivity`, `rate_limit`.\n- `SupervisorDecision`: `kind`, `reason`, `wait_seconds`, `capability`, `next_phase_repeats`.\n- `def snapshot(state: State) -> ProgressSnapshot: ...`\n- `def progress_fingerprint(state: State) -> str: ...`\n- `def decide(before: ProgressSnapshot, result: AttemptResult, retries: RetryState, policy: SupervisorPolicy, *, now: datetime) -> SupervisorDecision: ...`\n- `CapabilitySnapshot` is an immutable record with `required: bool`, `status: CapabilityStatus`, `latest_attempt_id: str | None`, and `latest_session_id: str | None`.\n- `ProgressSnapshot.drained` is derived only from `work.next_phase == \"\"` after the workflow drain transition.\n- `completed_prds == 0` defines an empty drain, including a batch where every attempted PRD was parked: no completed product work exists to send through post-drain QA.\n\nDetails:\n- Use canonical deterministic serialization for the workflow-only fingerprint; exclude raw revision, recovery fingerprint/repeats, control notices, and supervisor counters. A credible rate-limit reset is timezone-aware, strictly later than `now`, has delay at most `rate_limit_wait_seconds`, and remains inside the retry budget; connectivity and death use strict less-than retry-budget checks. Unchanged fingerprints return the incremented repeat count and compare it with `phase_repeat_limit`; changed fingerprints return zero repeats.\n- Encode the exact precedence and bounded retry outcomes specified by the design, including deterministic capability selection by lexicographically sorted name. Capability and completion rows are drained-only; a drained live-running capability halts; no-progress permission/authentication failures halt; empty drains skip only while required pending entries remain; unchanged successful sessions below the repeat limit return `RETRY`.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [P05-T01] Extract the post-session decision table as a pure function.\n- [P05-T03] Port state snapshot/progress/fingerprint logic.\n- a fake Claude driver drains build/review/done without Bash;\n- every continuation is explainable from state + summary;\n- the old Python loop's decision inventory is fully accounted for.\n\nVerify: focused decision tests cover every precedence row, retry boundary, fingerprint stability, empty/non-empty drain, capability terminality, and absence of final prose/provider-native inputs.\n",
