+      "description": "Implement durable provider-neutral capability execution\n\nAdd generic capability request/execution/runner/service APIs with session evidence, metrics, lifecycle validation, stale-owner reconciliation, and explicit retry.\n\nLocation: src/ovcaq/runtime/capability.py\n\nReuse: existing macOS process probes, SessionPaths/evidence helpers, FleetRegistry/process_matches identity checks, SessionMetric publication, and StateService compound methods.\n\nContract (verbatim \u2014 from the design doc's `## Interfaces & contracts`):\n- `CapabilityRequest`: `name`, `root`, `batch_id`, `attempt_id`, `session`, `timeout_seconds`.\n- `CapabilityExecution`: `success`, `session_id`, `detail`.\n- `class CapabilityRunner(Protocol): def run(self, request: CapabilityRequest) -> CapabilityExecution: ...`\n- `CapabilityService.start(self, name: str, *, expected_revision: int | None = None) -> CapabilityAttempt: ...`\n- `CapabilityService.finish(self, name: str, attempt_id: str, execution: CapabilityExecution, *, expected_revision: int | None = None) -> State: ...`\n- `CapabilityService.reconcile(self, name: str) -> State: ...`\n- `CapabilityService.retry(self, name: str, runner: CapabilityRunner) -> State: ...`\n- `start()` accepts only required `pending`, creates a globally unique attempt ID, appends exactly one `running` attempt, and atomically sets the capability `running`.\n- The explicit `retry()` entry point alone may advance `failed` to a new `running` attempt after ownership reconciliation; the supervisor loop exits nonzero on failure and never auto-retries it.\n- `reconcile()` treats a running attempt as live only when its retained session metadata still proves the owning PID identity; stale ownership becomes a failed attempt with actionable attention.\n- `CapabilityService` owns creation of the capability `SessionPaths`, its pending/final metric, runner invocation, raw evidence, and finalization for both the supervisor drain path and the standalone CLI re