+      "name": "Implement the foreground supervisor loop and effects",
+      "description": "Implement the foreground supervisor loop and effects\n\nImplement one no-TUI supervisor that launches fresh sessions, preserves raw evidence, reduces normalized results, applies one pure decision at a time, bounds retries/waits, and terminates with truthful state and metrics.\n\nLocation: src/ovcaq/runtime/supervisor.py; src/ovcaq/runtime/__init__.py\n\nReuse: RunLock/FleetRegistry/process_matches, OwnedProcess and supervisor signal helpers, Watchdog, session evidence/publication, driver LaunchRequest, reduce_session, workflow phase_complete/park/archive operations, decision.py, CapabilityService, and configuration routes.\n\nContract (verbatim \u2014 from the design doc's `## Interfaces & contracts`):\n- `class CapabilityRunnerResolver(Protocol): def __call__(self, capability: CapabilityEntry) -> CapabilityRunner: ...`\n- `SupervisorOutcome`: `exit_code`, `decision`, `sessions_attempted`.\n- `Supervisor.__init__(self, root: Path, *, store: StateStore, driver: AgentDriver, settings: SupervisorSettings, capability_runner: CapabilityRunnerResolver, clock: Clock, sleeper: Callable[[float], None]) -> None: ...`\n- `Supervisor.run(self) -> SupervisorOutcome: ...`\n- `Supervisor.run_once(self) -> AttemptResult: ...`\n- `Supervisor.apply(self, decision: SupervisorDecision) -> bool: ...`\n- `run()` acquires the existing `RunLock`, publishes fleet/run ownership, rejects unacknowledged emergency state failure, enters `supervisor_signal_scope()`, and loops until a terminal decision.\n- Each workflow attempt uses a fresh `SessionPaths`, `OwnedProcess.spawn(shell=False)`, `Watchdog`, raw-first `SessionEvidenceWriter`, driver decode, normalized observation persistence, driver summary, and `publish_session_summary()`.\n- Decode failures become `raw.unknown`/normalized failure evidence and do not crash the loop. A state read failure prevents another launch.\n- `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`/`SIGHUP` stop the owned process group, publish the terminal summary and metric, clean matching registry records, and return the shell-compatible signal exit code.\n\nDetails:\n- Reconcile metrics and stale capability ownership before launch; consume pause at a boundary and keep attention distinct from pause intent.\n- Reset retry counters only after changed workflow fingerprint or failure class, persist fingerprint/repeats by compare-and-set after decision, and retire the personal OS-notification path.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [P05-T04] Port bounded rate-limit, connectivity, death, park, and systemic-halt behavior using `SessionSummary`.\n- [P05-T05] Port pause, stop, drain, archive, metrics, and notification behavior.\n- [P05-T07] Implement `ovcaq run --no-tui` foreground supervisor.\n- a fake Claude driver drains build/review/done without Bash;\n- every continuation is explainable from state + summary;\n- the old Python loop's decision inventory is fully accounted for.\n\nVerify: focused supervisor tests cover productive nonzero exits, untouched success prose, rate-limit/connectivity/death bounds, repeat park/bootstrap pause, pause/stop/drain/archive, unknown decode, state failure, lock/signal/timeout cleanup, fresh sessions, capability handling, and exactly one finalized metric per attempt.\n",
