-      "name": "[D1] Correct Claude stream semantics and raw fallback evidence (L)",
-      "description": "What: Correct Claude stream semantics and raw fallback evidence (L)\n\nSource review: dev/local/reviews/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-review-1.md (HEAD 24fcec3bed6a41044c3d149d1f42bd678864e7e0)\n\nLocation:\n- src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py\n- src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py\n- src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\n- tests/drivers/test_claude.py\n- tests/drivers/test_claude_process.py\n- tests/events/test_tail.py\n- tests/fixtures/claude/v1/failures.jsonl\n- tests/fixtures/claude/v1/healthy.jsonl\n\nDetails:\nPort credible future timezone-qualified reset banners from the characterized source; vague, timezone-free, past or malformed values must not schedule retry. Only rejected rate-limit events represent an actual live limit; allowed_warning must remain observable without upgrading an unrelated failure to rate_limit. Preserve the five_hour versus seven_day distinction as normalized observation data for later policy, without embedding lifecycle decisions. Decode string/list/missing-content tool results with bounded sanitized details. Handle invalid UTF-8 at the raw framer with a true byte digest, while literal valid U+FFFD within valid JSON remains decodable. Mark message-derived cumulative usage estimated=true; an exact terminal snapshot contains only the provider-reported counters/cost and the shared reducer performs monotonic max/estimate precedence. Preserve bounded identity deduplication. Supply a required run_id to RawFirstDecoder, remember the last observed session_id for fallback, and use PROTOCOL_VERSION; update all callers. Add offset/naive timestamp cases and fail-first regressions for every behavior.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe0 High Rate-limit terminal banners are only classified and never parsed into a future timezone-qualified reset observation, so valid banner reset times cannot reach `SessionSummary.rate_limit_reset_at` as required | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:154 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: ALICE\n- \ud83d\udfe0 rate_limit_payload maps `allowed_warning` to rate_limit.started whatever the window, and drops rateLimitType. The reducer then turns any generic agent/unknown failure (or a missing terminal record) into RATE_LIMIT with the warning's reset, which can be days away for a seven_day warning. The source never treated allowed_warning as a limit: only `rejected` counts, and only a five_hour warning is a yield signal (usage_limit.py _warning_reset; golden 00199:41). So the port drops that five_hour/seven_day distinction and can make the supervisor wait out a weekly window after an unrelated failure | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:109 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 block_payload handles tool_result only when `content` is a string. List-form content (Task/subagent and MCP results) and missing content give no tool.completed/tool.failed, and a user record made only of such blocks becomes raw.unknown. The source render_stream._result_text joined the list's text blocks, and tracon retired lanes whatever the content shape | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:57 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 The `\"\\ufffd\" not in raw_line` guard sends any valid record containing a literal U+FFFD to raw.unknown (common in tool output decoded with replacement; a terminal result record lost this way makes the summary unsuccessful). The driver's raw_sha256 also hashes the re-encoded replaced text, not the raw bytes, so it can't be matched to the raw evidence | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:132 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 The Claude driver never sets estimated=True. Message-summed interim usage is inferred, yet it is reported as exact, and _update_usage folds message maxima into the \"exact\" result snapshot (the test expects cache_creation 6 against a reported 3). Plan \u00a711 says `estimated=true` is mandatory on inferred values, so the reducer's estimation logic is dead for the only real driver | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:299 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 RawFirstDecoder's fallback raw.unknown uses run_id=\"unknown\" and session_id=None (and a literal protocol_version=1 instead of PROTOCOL_VERSION), so oversized frames and frames the driver fails to decode drop the run's identity in normalized evidence | File: src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:103 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \u26aa The record_timestamp happy path is untested: a valid offset timestamp converted to UTC, and a naive timestamp falling back to now. The only parametrized cases are invalid values | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:10 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n- Preserve raw evidence, provider-neutral shared models, state authority and shell-free command construction.\n- Run focused regression tests and the work skill's mandatory final verification; do not perform completion review in the implementation session.\n",
