-      "name": "[D1] Document session ownership and cumulative observations (S)",
-      "description": "What: Document session ownership and cumulative observations (S)\n\nSource review: dev/local/reviews/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-review-1.md (HEAD 24fcec3bed6a41044c3d149d1f42bd678864e7e0)\n\nLocation:\n- docs/driver-protocol.md\n- dev/local/designs/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-design.md\n\nDetails:\nDocument one mutable driver decoder instance per session/run, and show a zero-argument DriverPlugin factory closure capturing fresh settings/run_id; the existing factory signature supports this, so do not invent a global registry or change the ABI. State that usage.updated carries cumulative per-session snapshots and how exact/estimated fieldwise-max reduction works. Clarify LaunchSpec.env as an overlay whose deliberate host merge is the later supervisor's responsibility. Update design notes for the reviewed corrections (configuration defaults, fallback_model/raw_format, explicit configured non-secret environment controls, raw fallback identity and writer naming), retaining the PRD's exact auto-only unattended launch contract. Do not edit the accepted umbrella implementation plan.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe1 Driver lifetime is not specified. ClaudeDriver.decode keeps per-session state (usage totals, session_id, a 1 MiB Bloom filter), but discovery builds one probed instance per name through a zero-argument DriverFactory, which cannot construct ClaudeDriver(settings, run_id=...). No built-in registration exists. Reusing one instance across sessions would inflate usage and leak the previous session_id into pre-init observations | File: docs/driver-protocol.md:18 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \u26aa The protocol doc doesn't say that usage.updated snapshots must be cumulative per session. The reducer folds fields by per-field max, so a per-turn delta driver (the Codex driver in PRD 00009) would undercount | File: docs/driver-protocol.md:18 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n- Preserve raw evidence, provider-neutral shared models, state authority and shell-free command construction.\n- Run focused regression tests and the work skill's mandatory final verification; do not perform completion review in the implementation session.\n",
