-      "name": "[D2] Fix Claude rate-limit reset and warning semantics (L)",
-      "description": "What: Fix Claude rate-limit reset and warning semantics (L)\n\nSource review: dev/local/reviews/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-review-2.md (HEAD b5ee110cc0c78ef0f886c49d433721e6e3d8f325)\n\nLocation:\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/docs/driver-protocol.md\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/drivers/test_claude_decode.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_reducer.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_model.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/fixtures/claude/v1/failures.jsonl\n\nContract (exact; the ObservationType enum stays closed, no new members):\n\n1. `rate_limit.started` payload shape becomes exactly {\"reset_at\", \"window\", \"detail\"}:\n   reset_at is an RFC 3339 UTC string or None (unchanged), window is a str or None\n   (provider-neutral window label, e.g. \"five_hour\", \"seven_day\"), detail is str.\n   `ovcaq.events.model` validates this shape (wrong key set -> ValueError; window\n   neither str nor None -> TypeError). docs/driver-protocol.md documents it.\n\n2. `ovcaq.drivers.claude_events.rate_limit_payload(info, now)` by `rate_limit_info.status`:\n   - \"rejected\" -> ObservationType.RATE_LIMIT_STARTED, payload\n     {\"reset_at\": <numeric resetsAt strictly after now as \"...Z\", else None>,\n      \"window\": <rateLimitType if str else None>, \"detail\": <sanitized text naming status and window>}.\n   - \"allowed_warning\" -> ObservationType.ACTIVITY_MESSAGE, payload\n     {\"kind\": \"rate_limit_warning\", \"window\": <str|None>, \"reset_at\": <same credible-future rule, else None>,\n      \"detail\": <sanitized text naming status and window>}.\n     It is NEVER rate_limit.cleared and NEVER rate_limit.started, so a warning never\n     clears an earlier rejected limit and never upgrades an unrelated failure to rate_limit.\n   - \"allowed\" -> ObservationType.RATE_LIMIT_CLEARED, payload {\"window\": <str|None>, \"detail\": ...}.\n   - any other status -> None (unchanged).\n\n3. Terminal banner reset parsing. Add a compiled module-level pattern in claude_events.py\n   (ported from the legacy source usage_limit.RESET_TIME, but with the zone group REQUIRED):\n     RESET_BANNER = re.compile(r\"resets\\s+(?:at\\s+)?(\\d{1,2})(?::(\\d{2}))?\\s*([ap]m)\\s*\\(([^)]+)\\)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n   and a function `banner_reset(text: str, anchor: datetime, now: datetime) -> str | None`:\n   - match RESET_BANNER; hour = int(h) % 12 (+12 for pm); minute = int(m or 0);\n   - zone = zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(group 4 stripped); unknown/invalid zone -> None;\n   - candidate = anchor.astimezone(zone) with that hour/minute, seconds 0; if candidate <= anchor-in-zone, add one day;\n   - return candidate in UTC as \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\" only when candidate > now, else None.\n   - no zone group (\"resets 8:10pm\", \"resets at 3pm\") -> no match -> None.\n   The anchor is the result record's own timestamp (record_timestamp of that record; now when absent).\n   The existing ISO-8601-with-offset banner form (\"resets 2100-01-01T02:00:00+02:00\") keeps working\n   with its current semantics; drop the synthetic `record_timestamp({\"timestamp\": ...})` reuse in favor of\n   a direct parse.\n\n4. ClaudeDriver precedence (per driver instance = per session): remember when this session has decoded a\n   rejected rate_limit_event. On a rate_limit terminal failure the driver emits\n   rate_limit.started {\"reset_at\": <banner reset>, \"window\": None, \"detail\": <failure detail>} ONLY when the\n   banner yields a credible future reset AND no rejected event was decoded earlier in this session.\n   session.failed(rate_limit) is still always emitted. Result: a rejected event's resetsAt wins over the banner.\n\nRequired regression behaviors (every one must fail before the fix):\n- rejected event (resetsAt 4102444800, rateLimitType five_hour) then a result banner\n  \"You've hit your usage limit \u00b7 resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)\" -> SessionSummary.rate_limit_reset_at == 2100-01-01T00:00:00Z.\n- rejected event then allowed_warning event then a generic agent failure result -> summary failure_class \"rate_limit\",\n  rate_limit_reset_at 2100-01-01T00:00:00Z (the warning does not clear the limit).\n- allowed_warning alone then a generic agent failure -> failure_class \"agent\", reset None; the warning is an\n  activity.message with kind \"rate_limit_warning\", window \"seven_day\"/\"five_hour\" as given, and its credible reset_at.\n- result record with \"timestamp\": \"2099-06-01T10:00:00Z\" and banner \"You've hit your session limit \u00b7 resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)\"\n  -> rate_limit.started reset_at \"2099-06-01T18:10:00Z\"; with anchor 2099-06-01T19:00:00Z -> \"2099-06-02T18:10:00Z\".\n- unknown zone \"(Mars/Olympus)\", zone-less \"resets 8:10pm\", and a past-resolving banner -> no rate_limit.started, reset None.\n- rejected event exposes window \"five_hour\" as structured payload data, not only prose.\n- a new failures.jsonl fixture line carries the real banner shape\n  {\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"error\",\"is_error\":true,\"session_id\":\"rate-limit-banner-session\",\"timestamp\":\"2099-06-01T10:00:00Z\",\"result\":\"You've hit your session limit \u00b7 resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)\"}\n  and the fixture matrix test asserts its reset.\nExisting tests that pin the old behavior (allowed_warning -> rate_limit.cleared; rate_limit.started keys {\"reset_at\",\"detail\"};\ncleared payload {\"detail\"}; the failure fixture's 7-line expectation) are updated to this contract.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe0 high `allowed_warning` emits `rate_limit.cleared` and can erase an earlier rejected limit | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:125 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: ALICE\n- \ud83d\udfe0 high Terminal banner overwrites a prior rejected event's credible reset with null | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:287 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe0 high Real `resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)` limit banners are not parsed | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:278 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium Rate-limit window and warning reset survive only as prose or are dropped | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:122 | Consensus: 1/3 | Found by: BOB\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n- Preserve raw evidence, provider-neutral shared models (no provider strings in events/), state authority.\n- Run focused regression tests and the work skill's mandatory final verification; do not perform completion review in the implementation session.\n",
