-      "description": "What: Bound normalized sanitizer cost and fallback preview (S)\n\nSource review: dev/local/reviews/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-review-3.md (HEAD ad892b3c2bb24086c1f6c973e5f7d0d9389dadd7)\n\nLocation:\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_model_rework.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_tail.py\n\nContract (exact):\n1. ovcaq.events.model._CREDENTIAL (src/ovcaq/events/model.py:24-29) must not start either prefix alternative with an unbounded `[\\w-]*`. Remove the leading `[\\w-]*` from both alternatives (the authorization/bearer one and the generic sensitive-word one). Measured at ad892b3: sanitize_text(\"a\" * n) took 0.22 s at 4 KB, 3.5 s at 16 KB, 14.3 s at 32 KB (quadratic).\n   - sanitize_text(\"a\" * 200_000) and sanitize_text(\"token\" * 40_000) each return in under 1 second (assert with time.perf_counter; generous bound).\n   - Every existing redaction test keeps passing unchanged, including key-prefixed forms: `x-api-key: <v>`, `my_token=<v>`, `HTTP_AUTHORIZATION: Bearer <v>`, JSON-looking `\"apiKey\": \"<v>\"` all leave no trace of <v>.\n2. RawFirstDecoder's raw.unknown fallback (src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:120-126) builds `preview` from a bounded window, never the whole retained frame:\n   - window = the first 4096 bytes of the retained buffer, decoded utf-8 with errors=\"replace\".\n   - If the window does not reach the true end of the frame (the retained buffer is longer than 4096 bytes, OR the frame exceeded max_frame_bytes so the buffer itself was cut), drop the trailing partial whitespace-delimited token from the window (cut at the last whitespace; if there is none, the window becomes empty).\n   - Then sanitize_text(window), then truncate to 512 characters. Preview length stays <= 512.\n   - Regression: with RawFirstDecoder(max_frame_bytes=512) and an oversized frame whose `Bearer <30+ [A-Za-z0-9_.-] chars>` or `sk-<20+ chars>` secret straddles the 512-byte cut, no prefix of the token (beyond the literal `Bearer ` / `sk-` marker) appears in the preview.\n   - Regression: an oversized 200 KB frame of unbroken word characters (e.g. b\"a\" * 200_000, no newline, default max_frame_bytes) fed then finished yields its raw.unknown in under 1 second.\n   Build synthetic secrets by string concatenation (the repo secret scanner blocks literal credentials), following test_model_rework.py.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe0 high `sanitize_text` is quadratic on long unbroken `[\\w-]` runs (leading `[\\w-]*` in both `_CREDENTIAL` prefix alternatives backtracks); task 17's sanitize-first fix widened the raw.unknown preview input from 512 bytes to the whole frame (up to 1 MiB), so one bad frame can stall decoding for hours | File: src/ovcaq/events/model.py:25 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: EVE\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium With `max_frame_bytes=512` the retained buffer can end mid-secret before redaction, so the preview exposes a prefix at the frame boundary | File: src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:123 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: BOB\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n- Run focused regression tests and the work skill's mandatory final verification; do not perform completion review in the implementation session.\n",
