-      "description": "What: Fix rate-limit banner precedence and dated banners (S)\n\nSource review: dev/local/reviews/00006-events-claude-adapter-v1-review-3.md (HEAD ad892b3c2bb24086c1f6c973e5f7d0d9389dadd7)\n\nLocation:\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py\n- /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/docs/driver-protocol.md\n- the existing Claude decoder rate-limit test module under /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/drivers/\n\nContract (exact):\n1. Banner precedence (claude.py:67, :189-192, :281). Keep the live-limit flag semantics (set by a rejected event, cleared by a later `allowed`, untouched by `allowed_warning`), with ONE change: a rejected event sets the flag only when its projected payload carries a non-null (credible, future) reset_at. The terminal-result banner is parsed and emits `rate_limit.started` iff the flag is False.\n   Required sequences (summary = driver.summarize over the decoded observations):\n   - rejected(credible R) -> allowed_warning -> banner B: no banner-derived rate_limit.started; summary reset == R.\n   - rejected(credible R) -> allowed -> banner B: the limit was cleared, so the banner applies: one banner-derived rate_limit.started with B; summary reset == B. (Revised 2026-09-30 after Devon showed the earlier contract forced a cleared limit to drive the retry time; review finding M1 is discarded.)\n   - rejected(no resetsAt, or a past resetsAt) -> banner B: banner rate_limit.started IS emitted; summary reset == B.\n   - allowed_warning(future resetsAt) alone -> banner B: banner started with B; summary reset == B.\n   - allowed alone -> banner B: summary reset == B.\n   - rejected(credible R) -> banner B: unchanged, summary reset == R.\n   - no rate_limit_event -> banner B: unchanged, summary reset == B.\n2. Dated banners (claude_events.py:150 RESET_BANNER, banner_reset). Also accept an optional date prefix: `resets <Mon> <D> at <h>[:<mm>]<am|pm> (<IANA zone>)`, month as a 3-letter English abbreviation (Jan..Dec, case-insensitive), day 1-31, e.g. `resets Sep 20 at 11am (Europe/Prague)`. Resolve it on the anchor's local year in that zone; if that wall time is <= the anchor's local time, use the next year. Invalid input returns None: Feb 30, Sep 31, day 0 or 32, Feb 29 in a non-leap resolved year (Feb 29 resolves in a leap year), hour 13+ or minute 60+. All twelve months Jan..Dec parse. Time-only banners keep today's behavior. The result must still be future relative to `now` or None.\n3. Docs (docs/driver-protocol.md, near line 55): state that a provider `allowed_warning` arrives as `activity.message` with payload kind `rate_limit_warning` (fields window, reset_at, detail) and never as `rate_limit.cleared`; state the banner rule from item 1 in one sentence.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium `rejected \u2192 allowed \u2192 banner`: clearing `_limit_live` lets the banner emit a new `rate_limit.started`, though task 16 says \"no rejected event decoded earlier in this session\" | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:191 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium Dated weekly banners (`resets Sep 20 at 11am (Europe/Prague)`) do not match `RESET_BANNER`, so multi-day limits carry no reset | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:150 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: EVE\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium A rejected event with no credible reset still suppresses a credible banner reset (summary keeps null); narrows the literal task-16 wording | File: src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:189 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: EVE\n- \u26aa low Protocol doc does not describe `allowed_warning` as `activity.message` kind `rate_limit_warning` | File: docs/driver-protocol.md:55 | Consensus: 1/5 | Found by: ALICE\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n- Run focused regression tests and the work skill's mandatory final verification; do not perform completion review in the implementation session.\n",
