ary outcome from the code and docs, do not change the code). Extend docs/driver-protocol.md:62-63 to name this sequence and its outcome.\n4. Add tests: the Feb 29 non-leap-anchor case returns None (fails against HEAD 82a12fe), and the leap-anchor case returns the 2096 instant.\n\nAcceptance: every quoted finding no longer reproduces.\n\n### Findings (verbatim)\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium | Invalid dates advance to the next year: `resets Feb 29 at 9am (UTC)` anchored 2095-01-10 returns 2096 instead of None | src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:205 | [1/5] BOB\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium | `rejected(credible R) -> rejected(no reset) -> banner B` is unpinned by a test and undocumented | src/ovcaq/drivers/claude.py:190 | [1/5] EVE\n- \ud83d\udfe1 medium | Time-only branch builds the same `datetime(...)` twice; simplify | src/ovcaq/drivers/claude_events.py:206 | [1/5] ALICE\n- \u26aa low | Feb 29 fall-through from a non-leap anchor year is untested | tests/drivers/test_claude_rate_limit.py:361 | [1/5] EVE\n",
